 {"id":"OBS-OB-001","title":"[P1] Minimal viable Prometheus emission: /metrics/prom with 5 series via client_golang+promhttp","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"lane":"monitoring","type":"task","created_by":"monitoring-lane","source":"obs-audit-2026-11-03","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T18:08:14Z","attempts":0,"capability_tags":["observability","prometheus","metrics-endpoint"],"reasoning":"WHY: the lab is currently unobservable by any collector. It HAS a metrics route (internal/api/server.go:118 mux.HandleFunc(\"GET /metrics\", s.handleMetrics)) but handleMetrics (server.go:313-320) serves writeJSON of a bespoke metrics.Snapshot (internal/metrics/metrics.go:219-252): no Prometheus client library exists anywhere in the repo (grep -rn 'prometheus|promhttp|client_golang' over *.go/*.mod = 0 hits), no /metrics text format, and no scrape job. Live proof of the cost: GET :8766/metrics returns skipped_host_pressure=89, solve_count=0, while /api/v1/stats returns queue_depth=20 - the loop has been gate-skipping every tick for 1h29m of uptime at load1=14.77 against -load-threshold 4 (deploy/off-by-one.service:62) and nothing alerts. WHY THESE 5 FIRST: they answer the only 3am question that matters - is it up, is it doing work, is work backing up. WHAT: add prometheus/client_golang + promhttp to go.mod; register a PRIVATE registry on api.Server (do NOT use the global default registry and do NOT register NewGoCollector - the fleet already drowns in ~2000 self/exporter families for ~20 real app series); serve promhttp.HandlerFor(reg) at a NEW path GET /metrics/prom (leave the existing JSON /metrics byte-identical - docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md:1075-1116 and docs/dogfood/2026-10-16-operator-integration.md:25,48,92 consume it). Emit: obo_http_up (gauge), obo_cron_loop_running (gauge, false when main.go:225 'cron loop not started' fires), obo_solves_total{outcome=succeeded|failed|rejected} (counter - wired from internal/cron/loop.go:101-117 Metrics, which today is computed and exposed NOWHERE: the comment at loop.go:174-176 says it is what the endpoint 'will eventually expose' but handleMetrics never reads it), obo_queue_pending (gauge from queue.go:646-652 Depth via the status breakdown), obo_solve_duration_seconds{outcome} histogram with buckets 30,60,120,180,300,600,1200,2400 (observed mean is 226.2s over 3354 completed solves). Spec: docs/observability-spec.md sections 3.1, 4.1, 4.2. ACCEPTANCE: (1) `curl -s -D- http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom | head -3` returns HTTP 200 with `Content-Type: text/plain; version=0.0.4` and at least one line beginning `# HELP obo_`. (2) `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom | grep -c '^obo_'` >= 5 and the body contains obo_http_up 1, obo_cron_loop_running 1, obo_solves_total, obo_queue_pending, and obo_solve_duration_seconds_bucket. (3) the existing JSON surface is unchanged: `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics | jq -e .skipped_host_pressure` succeeds and returns the same numeric type as before. (4) obo_queue_pending equals `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/api/v1/stats | jq .queue_depth`. (5) `go test ./internal/api/ ./internal/cron/` passes and a new test asserts the text exposition parses (e.g. via expfmt.TextParser) with zero malformed lines.","acceptance_criteria":"curl -s -D- http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom returns 200 + Content-Type text/plain; version=0.0.4 and >=5 obo_* families including obo_http_up, obo_cron_loop_running, obo_solves_total, obo_queue_pending, obo_solve_duration_seconds; obo_queue_pending == /api/v1/stats .queue_depth; JSON /metrics unchanged; go test ./internal/api/ ./internal/cron/ green.","detail":{"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md","sections":["3.1","4.1","4.2"],"blind_spot":"loop starvation invisible; cron.Metrics dead code"},"commit_hash":"62b1c03b74304faf66e2e2fd2cf399f070034a30","completed_at":"2026-11-04T18:08:14Z","guard_result":"go build ./... + go vet ./... OK; go test ./internal/api/ ./internal/cron/ ./internal/metrics/ ok; live /metrics/prom verified on :8766","judge":"PASS e7a8d974 (tier2 PASS at 62b1c03b, judged 2026-11-04 by an earlier tick that left the row pending)","worker_summary":"Reconciliation close, no new implementation. The feature shipped in feat 62b1c03b (ancestor of tag v0.3.0 031733b7) and its gitreins tier2 verdict passed (history dir e7a8d974), but the row was never flipped, so every census counted it as an open P1 (see RELEASE-OB-020). This tick additionally proved it LIVE for the first time, because the live binary now carries the code: curl :8766/metrics/prom -> 200, Content-Type text/plain; version=0.0.4, 5 # HELP obo_ families (obo_http_up 1, obo_cron_loop_running 1, obo_solves_total, obo_queue_pending 40, obo_solve_duration_seconds 33 bucket lines); JSON /metrics .skipped_host_pressure still 1; obo_queue_pending 40 == .queue_depth 40."}
 {"id":"OBS-OB-002","title":"[P2] Emit gate/scheduler health: skip reasons, host load/memory, last-tick freshness","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"lane":"monitoring","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:34Z","capability_tags":["observability","cron","starvation","alerting"],"reasoning":"WHY: OBS-OB-001 makes the loop's liveness visible but not its STARVATION. The single most damaging failure mode of this product is alive-but-not-working: at audit time the loop had skipped every tick for 1h29m (skipped_host_pressure=89, last_skip_reason='load', load1=14.77). The reason vocabulary already exists and is already normalised - metrics.TrimSpaceReason (internal/metrics/metrics.go:309-314) yields exactly 'load', 'memory', 'load+memory' - and the host reading is already captured in HostSnapshot (metrics.go:70-76: Load1, MemUsedFraction, MemTotalBytes, MemAvailableBytes, Reason) via RecordSkip/RecordHost (metrics.go:150-172, called from cron/loop.go:580 and :590). All of it is discarded into a JSON string. Nothing measures loop FRESHNESS, so a hung loop that still answers HTTP looks identical to a healthy one. WHAT: emit obo_cron_ticks_total{outcome=deferred|attempted|empty}; obo_cron_skip_reason_total{reason=load|memory|load+memory} (cardinality 3, closed set - never a free-text reason); obo_host_load1 (gauge) and obo_host_mem_used_fraction (gauge 0-1) as the last gate reading, mirroring HostSnapshot; obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds (gauge, unix seconds, set on every tick regardless of outcome - this is what distinguishes a hung loop from a gated one). Add one alert rule (owned by the monitoring stack, not this repo): fire when sum(rate(obo_cron_skip_reason_total[30m])) > 0 AND sum(rate(obo_solves_total[1h])) == 0 AND time() - obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds < 180 (i.e. ticking, gated, producing nothing). Spec: docs/observability-spec.md sections 3.2 and 4.3. ACCEPTANCE: (1) `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom | grep -E 'obo_(cron_skip_reason_total|host_load1|cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds|cron_ticks_total)'` returns all four families. (2) `obo_host_load1` is within 5% of `cat /proc/loadavg | cut -d' ' -f1`. (3) starvation is provably detectable: restart the service with `-load-threshold 0.1`, wait 3 cron intervals, then `obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds` must ADVANCE while `obo_cron_skip_reason_total{reason=\"load\"}` also advances - two facts that together are the alert condition; restore the unit's -load-threshold 4 afterwards. (4) `obo_cron_skip_reason_total` label values are a subset of {load,memory,load+memory} - assert in a Go test that iterates all recorded reasons (no free text can reach the label).","acceptance_criteria":"/metrics/prom exposes obo_cron_skip_reason_total, obo_cron_ticks_total, obo_host_load1, obo_host_mem_used_fraction, obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds; obo_host_load1 within 5% of /proc/loadavg field 1; with -load-threshold 0.1 the last-tick timestamp advances while skip_reason_total{reason=\"load\"} advances; label values subset of the 3-value vocabulary.","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"8da6b933","ts":"2026-11-16T22:57:34Z"}],"sections":["3.2","4.3"],"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md"},"commit_hash":"6c4e09aa54d7813b50fa0b866fa9b7a069bdfb8c","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Judge PASS verdict 8da6b933 (tier1+tier2) on HEAD 6c4e09aa: five scheduler-health families live on /metrics/prom, closed outcome vocabulary solved|empty|idle_gated|error per observability-spec 3.2, load1 0% delta vs /proc/loadavg, skip_reason{load}+last_tick advance under forced 0.1 threshold, Go closed-set tests PASS, full suite 16 pkgs ok, :8766 unit untouched. Criterion provisional (deferred|attempted) wording corrected to spec vocabulary before re-judge (525f2b94 FAIL = wording-only). Landed by crashed sibling session; lifecycle finished by this tick."}
