 {"id":"QA-OFF-BY-ONE-5-R3","title":"[P3] RECURRENCE of QA-OFF-BY-ONE-5, new arm — chaos-disconnect grades OK on a Go toolchain refusal (GOTOOLCHAIN=local, bootstrap go 1.26.5 below go.mod floor 1.26.9): the app never started, so disconnect resilience is still unverified","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T19:14:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:50Z","capability_tags":["qa-harness","false-green","chaos"],"reasoning":"MEASURED clean-machine battery off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03 (agent cf73b3aa, hermes-fleet-03, tested SHA 6546b59e00cce3085e1a003bbfe736c0f51db379, clone at that SHA, origin github.com/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one, clean).\nCell detail verbatim: chaos-disconnect OK 'chaos-disconnect tests: fails fast on disconnect (rc=1): go: go.mod requires go >= 1.26.9 (running go 1.26.5; GOTOOLCHAIN=local)'.\nPer-cell log /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03/harvest/qa-logs-2320801/disc.log contains ONLY that one line — no app start, no disconnect trace.\nROOT CAUSE reproduced on the agent: go.mod line 3 is 'go 1.26.9'; the battery bootstrap installs /home/kara/tools/go/bin/go with GOVERSION go1.26.5 (built Jul 1); the chaos probe runs with GOTOOLCHAIN=local GOPROXY=off by design (bunker-qa.sh:3043), so the build refuses before main() runs. With GOTOOLCHAIN=local 'go build ./...' exits 1 with the same message; with GOTOOLCHAIN=auto (the fresh-install cell's mode) the toolchain is downloaded and the tree builds — which is why fresh-install is OK and only the local-pinned chaos probe dies.\nConsequence: the rc=1 that the classifier reads as 'fails fast on disconnect' is a compile refusal. Same defect family as QA-OFF-BY-ONE-5 / -R2 (a non-disconnect failure scored as an OK disconnect verdict); new arm is the toolchain floor, not ENOSPC. Product disconnect behaviour remains UNVERIFIED.","acceptance_criteria":"Kill the false green at its cause, not in the evidence file. Either (a) the batt