 {"id":"OB-OPS-006","title":"off-by-one daemon owns a live SQLite graph store with no backup or restore path (ops census backup P1)","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-07T20:22:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T20:47:38Z","capability_tags":[],"reasoning":"Measured by the fleet-ops-check tick fleet-ops-check-2026-11-07-16-20-57 on an unattended api_server surface.\n\nCensus: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project off-by-one --json -> rc=1, kind=service, gap '[P1] backup: owns a datastore with no backup/restore path'.\n\nInstrument is partly a false positive and the refutation matters: two of the three hit paths are NOT the trigger. .coding-hermes/board/schema.sql is the foreman board's own DDL (canonical board is git-tracked JSONL) - refuted. The real store is separate: cmd/off-by-one/main.go:415 opens envString(\"OFF_BY_ONE_DB\", \"./off-by-one.db\") through graph.Open(*cfg.dbPath), seeded from the tracked schema sql/schema/schema.sql (sqlite/Postgres-compatible DDL for problem_classes + lateral edges). A running daemon is live right now: PID 1871714 /home/kara/off-by-one/off-by-one --port 8766 -cron-interval 60s. Whereas most families only have the board-schema false positive, here the database is the lab's product (solved corpus + graph edges), is gitignored (*.db in .gitignore:22), and git ls-files shows NO backup/restore artifact (the only 'restore' hits are answer-corpus JSON filenames). So a disk loss destroys the accumulated solve graph with no procedure to recover it.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n1. scripts/backup-db.sh exists, takes the db path from OFF_BY_ONE_DB (default ./off-by-one.db), writes a timestamped dump to a configurable destination, and is safe to run against a LIVE database (sqlite3 .backup / VACUUM INTO - never cp of a live file).\n2. The script self-verifies: a --drill arm restores the newest dump into a throwaway database and compares table row counts (must exit 0 and print the compared counts).