+{"id":"OB-OPS-007","title":"[P0] Solver was DEAD for ~12h: /tmp/pi was wiped and the daemon silently skipped the ro-bind — every solve failed with 'pi binary not found' and was recorded as a bare solver_exit","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":3,"type":"ops","lane":"ops","created_by":"foreman","created_at":"2026-11-17T16:10:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T16:10:00Z","completed_at":"2026-11-17T16:10:00Z","commit_hash":"none:host-state-restore","reasoning":"WHY: the pre-solve lab could not solve anything. Evidence chain: (1) journal, live PID 1871714, minute cadence — `cron: solve failed for sub_xxx: pi-agent exec: exit status 1` starting before this tick; (2) after the tick's deploy restart the new binary logged exactly one `note: /tmp/pi not present — skipping ro-bind (solver wrapper install location)` and a scratch instance then printed `pi-agent: pi binary not found — install from https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/releases`, failing 16 solves in 30s as cause=solver_exit; (3) /tmp/pi did not exist while pi-agent's resolver (/home/kara/.local/bin/pi-agent findPiBin) looks for an ELF at $PI_BIN, ~/.local/bin/pi, ~/.local/lib/pi/pi, /tmp/pi/pi and a monorepo layout at /tmp/pi or ~/.local/share/pi — none of which existed. /tmp is volatile, so this class recurs on any /tmp cleanup or reboot, and cmd/off-by-one/main.go:607-610 only Logf's a soft note instead of failing closed, which is why it rotted silently while the queue grew to 52 pending.","detail":{"trigger":"/tmp wiped (volatile solver install location)","fix_applied":"copied the durable release ELF /home/kara/.local/share/pi-elf/pi (106MB, Oct 7) to /tmp/pi/pi, chmod 755, then restarted the daemon so the conditional ro-bind takes effect","proof":"scratch instance on a DB copy with -load-threshold -1 reached a real pi-agent solve that ran until the 20s --solve-timeout kill (journal: 'solve killed by --solve-timeout 20s: pi-agent exec: signal: killed', cause=timeout) — the wrapper now RESOLVES and EXECUTES pi instead of erroring","residual":"the ELF reports --version 0.0.0 while the host npm install is 1.5.0; version parity with the host pi was not established"},"acceptance_criteria":"The solver install location must be durable and its absence must be loud. (a) The daemon resolves pi from a path that survives /tmp cleanup (a durable ELF under $HOME or an explicit PI_BIN in the unit), OR the startup path re-materialises /tmp/pi from a durable source; (b) a missing solver is a startup ERROR (nonzero exit / refused start) or a FAILING check, never a soft `note:` log line; (c) `make check-deploy` (or a new `make check-solver`) FAILS when the resolved pi is absent or unexecutable, and PASSES once it is present; (d) a scratch solve on a DB copy completes or is killed by its own timeout — never `pi binary not found`. Prove by running the new check against a tree where /tmp/pi is absent (expect FAIL naming the missing solver) and present (expect PASS), plus one real scratch solve that reaches pi-agent.","foreman_note":"Tick's biggest find; fixed live in-tick (host state, not repo code). Filed so the durability half lands as code: the soft note is the defect that hid a 12h outage.","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"Host-state repair + evidence; the durable/loud-fail half is the acceptance criteria above.","guard_result":"n/a (host state)"}
